# This repository is checked out with core.autocrlf=true. Artifacts whose
# SHA-256 is recorded as their identity must therefore be exempted from
# end-of-line conversion, or a fresh checkout would rewrite their bytes and
# invalidate every recorded digest.
#
# The manual-review workspace is generated with LF-only bytes and is verified by
# comparing raw bytes against a fresh regeneration, so it is locked here.
# It is machine-generated and never hand-edited, so suppressing conversion in
# both directions is what byte identity means for it.
results/annotations/** -text

# The tracked specifications are also identified by their LF bytes: the accepted
# digest of the manual-review course protocol is computed over them, and
# tests/test_reporting_doc_references.py parses one of them untranslated. Unlike
# the generated workspace above these are hand-edited, so -text would be the
# wrong tool -- it would let a CRLF working copy write CRLF straight into the
# index and break the recorded digest permanently. Normalizing to LF on the way
# in and checking out LF on the way out protects both directions.
docs/specs/** text eol=lf
